  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "One candle is 15 cm long and takes 4 hours to burn completely. A second candle is 20 cm long and takes 3 hours to burn completely. If both candles are lit at the same time, find the time taken for the second candle to be exactly 1 cm shorter than the first candle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{72}{35}$ hours.",
      "worked": "The burn rates are $\\dfrac{15}{4}$ cm/hour and $\\dfrac{20}{3}$ cm/hour. After $t$ hours, the heights are $15-\\dfrac{15}{4}t$ cm and $20-\\dfrac{20}{3}t$ cm. The second height must be 1 cm less than the first.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}20-\\frac{20}{3}t&=15-\\frac{15}{4}t-1\\\\240-80t&=168-45t\\\\240&=168+35t\\\\72&=35t\\\\t&=\\frac{72}{35}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe second candle is 1 cm shorter than the first after $\\dfrac{72}{35}$ hours.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
